      n: 54, title: 'More of the gluttons — Bonagiunta and the "sweet new style"', tourTitle: 'Bonagiunta and the dolce stil novo', hook: 'Forese Donati names the souls of the gluttons, including Pope Martin IV. Then Bonagiunta of Lucca raises the question of Dante\'s new poetic style — the sweet new style.',
      tour: `More of the sixth terrace. Forese names the souls: Pope Martin IV (who loved Bolsena eels and Vernaccia wine), Ubaldino della Pila, Boniface of Fiesole, Marchese of Forlì. Then Bonagiunta da Lucca, an earlier Italian poet, speaks to Dante about the sweet new style — asking whether Dante is the one who brought the new rhymes that began "Ladies who have intelligence of love." Dante explains: the dolce stil novo takes dictation from love. Bonagiunta acknowledges that he and his school were restrained from this by something that tied down his pen. Forese prophecies that Dante will see Piccarda in Paradise; then he runs on.`,
